Clados 

* Packages

	<<Name>> : <<Purpose>>

	* cladosG : Geometry 

	* cladosF : Numbers

	* cladosGExceptions : Geometry related exceptions

	* cladosfExceptions : Number related exceptions

	[]

	<<<Clados is a set of java packages implementing multi-vectors and multi-vector lists in Clifford Algebras.>>>

	If you don't know what a Clifford Algebra is, you are encouraged to read about them.  
	Geometric Algebras are also Clifford Algebras and provide geometry modeling choice variations, 
	so don't bypass content describing them either. They all offer a tidy mathematical formalism 
	combining many disparate tools of geometry enabling one to wield them in algebraic ways. 

	The best way get started nowadays is to drop by the {{{https://bivector.net/}Bivector.net}} Discord Server.\
	There is also a lot of recent You-Tube content ranging from teaching material from {{{https://www.youtube.com/@sudgylacmoe/videos}sudgylacmoe}} \
	to research grade references from {{{https://www.youtube.com/@eigenchris}eigenchris}} \
	and many others, but many of the creators and code writers can be found on the Discord server.

* Project History

	The tools contained in this library evolved from work done at UC Davis between the late 1970's 
	and early 1990's. It is intended to support physical models that rely upon geometry in the style 
	taught by Prof. Ken Greider.

	The word 'Clados' is an acronym for CLifford Algebra Derived ObjectS. It was chosen to avoid math 
	library name collisions and because it comes close to the concept of 'clade' which this author 
	finds apropos for multivectors.

	Basic and complete geometric objects are modeled by the Monad class which most people think of 
	as 'Multivector.' A modeling requirement for aggregates of multivectors drove the main decision 
	to use 'Monad' instead because 'Mult-multivector' is a mouthful. 

	Nyads are Monad aggregates and are modeled as lists. Lists of increasing size form a series
	\{Monad, Dyad, Triad, Tetrad, ...\}, so there is some sense to our naming convention. 
	However, for implementors not interested in aggregates, the name 'Monad' is unfortunate. 
	Please treat it as a synonym for multivector.

	{{{./ProgressIndicator.html}Progress Signs}}

* Documentation 

** Usage And API

	Work has begun on usage documentation to replace the old project book listed below. Don't 
	expect a lot yet. Seriously. The work is only just getting underway.

	{{{./Connections.html}Using the new Connection Class}}

	The primary use case for Clados is as a low level geometry library, so the API documentation
	is critical. When used properly, a library user should never have to concern themselves with 
	<<how>> Clifford algebras are represented. Intead they may focus on <<how>> geometry is 
	represented and then folded into physical simulations. 
	
	The API docs show which classes are present and how to interact with them, but private
	elements and methods do most of the low level work where they are intentionally kept out of
	reach of most library users. One may look at the code directly, but one should never have to 
	worry about how blade multiplication works especially when it comes to bit key handling.

	{{{./apidocs/index.html}API v2.0}}

